 "notes": [
  "PrimeOne (MI) divestiture completed in Q4-24 (no held-for-sale balances at year end); MI gain on dispositions $38M in Q4. ES segment printed with zero.",
  "IS \"(Gain) loss on dispositions, net\" printed (38) -> gain_disp +38. \"Other (income) expense, net\" printed (14) -> oth_inc +14. Segment-table total expenses 2,283 = IS expenses 2,333 - gain 38 - equity income 12.",
  "New in Q4-24: deal-related amortization of 6 is also adjusted in \"Other (income) expense, net\" (Exhibit 5 Adjusted Other (Income) Expense). deal_amort_pre = OP-level deal amortization 288 + 6 = 294 (ties to after-tax 222 + tax 72); seg/corp/equity-income deal amortization lines unaffected.",
  "MI and Mobility \"liability write-off\" of $1M recorded as a benefit (pre -1): the release does not state the sign, but MI items (42 - 38 + 7 - 4 + 3 = 10) only tie to printed MI adjustment 9 with the write-off as a benefit. Mobility write-off after-tax \"less than $1 million\" -> net 0; CORP net acquisition-related benefit $1M after-tax \"less than $1 million\" -> net 0.",
  "Executive Leadership Team transition costs (MI $3M, CORP $5M) categorized SEVER per schema.",
  "TAX item (footnote i): tax expense of $1M due to annualized effective tax rate differences for GAAP (+1).",
  "Item after-tax sum 62 vs printed aggregate 61 (rounding); 880 + 61 + 222 = 1,163.",
  "ngaap.items_total_pre = operating-level \"Non-GAAP adjustments\" (80); interest adjustment (premium amortization benefit, footnote h) printed separately as 6 (adjusted interest 75 vs GAAP 69).",
  "Non-GAAP adjusted tax line: non-GAAP adjustments 12, deal-related amortization 72. adj_oth_inc = adjusted other (income) expense printed (20) -> +20.",
  "cfpub: twelve-month (ytd 12); capex and nci_dist positive outflows; three-month FCF in fcf_pub_q / adj_fcf_pub_q.",
  "FY2025 guidance; Exhibit 8 bridge: deal amortization 2.91, premium amortization benefit (0.07), tax rate and other (0.04). Guidance now gives operating profit margin levels (not expansion).",
  "No organic/constant-currency table."
 ],
